      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "the swan only of the luxury of residing in a bed of lotus",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "plants; but he cannot rob the bird of his universal reputation",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "for skill in separating milk from water.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "19. Bracelets do not beautify a person, nor do necklaces",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "resplendent like the moon, nor bathing, nor anointing ( with",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "rubbed sandal &c), nor (wearing) flowers, nor bedecked hair.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "Speech alone beautifies a person when it is possessed in a",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "refined form. (Other) ornaments wear away continuously; the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "ornament of speech is the (only) one which lasts for ever.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "20. Learning is verily the highest (mark of or, addition-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "al ) beauty for man; it is a treasure concealed and well-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "protected; it places within his reach enjoyments, honour and",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "happiness; it is an object of reverence even to those who are",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "worthy of reverence; while journeying in strange lands it is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "a friend; and it is the highest deity; learning is honoured by",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "kings, but not wealth; one destitute of learning is a beast.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "21. If men have forgiveness, why should they require",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "an armour; no (other) enemies (are required to ruin) them",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "if they are hot-tempered; if there are kins-people, where is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "the necessity of fire ? ( i. e. they will do the destructive work",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "of fire ); if there is a friend, what use is there of medicines",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "of sovereign virtue ? What need is there of serpents if",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "wicked men (exist) ? Of what account is wealth if there is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "blamaless learning ? What is the use of ornaments if (one",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "has) (a proper sense of ) shame ? If there is sweet poesy, of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "what good is a kingdom ?",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "22. The stability of the world solely depends on those",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "men who are expert in the following arts:—courtesy to-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "wards one’s relations, kindness towards strangers, cunning",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "towards the wicked, affection for virtuous men, policy to-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "wards princes, humility towards the learned, bravery in",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
